      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-322737",
      ":question/problem": "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{\u2032}(t)=-6{x}_{1}(t)+7{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{\u2032}(t)=-2{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs above, where $t\\in R.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below. $\\,$ The function $a(t)=[\\begin{aligned}7{e}^{-4t} \\\\ 2{e}^{-4t}\\end{aligned}]$ \n{{field-1}} \na solution of the system.\n\n$\\,$ The function $b(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ -2{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]$ \n{{field-2}} \na solution of the system.\n\n$\\,$ The function $c(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]$ \n{{field-3}} \na solution of the system.\n\n$\\,$ {{field-4}} \nis a set of fundamental solutions to the system because the Wronskian \n\n$$\nW({{field-5}})={{field-6}}\\ne 0\n$$\n\n$\\,$ for at least one $t\\in R.$"
