      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-334527",
      ":question/problem": "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{\u2032}(t)=-3{x}_{1}(t)-3{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{\u2032}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs above, where $t\\in R.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below.$\\,$ The function $a(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1-3t \\\\ 3t\\end{aligned}]$  \n{{field-1}}  \na solution of the system.\n\n$\\,$ The function $b(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2(1-3t) \\\\ 6t\\end{aligned}]$  \n{{field-2}}  \na solution of the system.\n\n$\\,$ The function $c(t)=[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ t\\end{aligned}]$  \n{{field-3}}  \na solution of the system.\n\n$\\,$ {{field-4}}  \ndoes not give a set of fundamental solutions to the system because the Wronskian  \n\n$$\nW({{field-5}})={{field-6}}\n$$\n\n$\\,$ for all $t\\in R.$"
